# ===========================================================================
#  _headers - security headers for the PUBLISHED site
# ===========================================================================
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#  --------------------
#  Locally, server.js sends the site's security headers. When the site is
#  published to a static host, server.js is NOT deployed - the host serves
#  the files in public/ directly - so those headers would silently vanish.
#  The site would look identical while losing its Content-Security-Policy,
#  its clickjacking protection and its referrer policy.
#
#  This file re-declares them for the host. It is read by GitLab Pages,
#  Netlify and Cloudflare Pages, all of which use the same format. The host
#  consumes the file and does not serve it to visitors.
#
#  KEEP IT IN STEP WITH server.js
#  ------------------------------
#  The securityHeaders() function in server.js is the source of truth and
#  explains what each header does. The values below are copied from it
#  verbatim. `npm run test:links` fails if a header exists in server.js but
#  is missing here, so the two cannot silently drift apart.
#
#  FORMAT: a path pattern on its own line, then indented "Name: value"
#  lines. /* matches every path on the site.
# ===========================================================================

/*
  # media-src includes blob: because hls.js feeds video to the player through
  # Media Source Extensions, which uses a locally-created blob: URL. It does
  # not allow media from any external origin.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(self), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off

  # HTTP Strict Transport Security: tells browsers to only ever reach this
  # site over HTTPS. server.js deliberately never sends this locally, because
  # it would pin http://127.0.0.1 to HTTPS and break other local projects.
  #
  # Now set to a full year, having confirmed HTTPS works on both
  # patrickmills.dev and www.patrickmills.dev with a valid certificate.
  #
  # CAUTION if you ever change this: max-age is in seconds and browsers
  # REMEMBER it. A visitor who loads the site once will refuse to reach it
  # over plain HTTP for a year afterwards. Lowering the number here does not
  # un-remember it for people who have already visited. Only raise it again
  # after HTTPS is known good - which it is.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
